index.html: viewport opts into safe-area values and Android browser chrome uses the maroon theme color; styles are cache-versioned to revision 23 and scripting to revision 13; the invitee carousel contains six accessible cards, including Marathi captions for Neha and Kaustubh after the mother, Kaku-Dada-Vahini as the fourth card, the five-cat card using Mika22 with the shared pet-tile sizing, and the two-photo Anya card with Anya2 as the larger solo portrait; the venue page has a centered ceremonial header with matching watercolor kalash and havankund artwork, a compact baraat banner, akshada-framed venue name, structured date/muhurat/address facts with an embedded Marathi parking and valet note, and Google Maps icon action
styles.css: the centered wedding framing has a sequenced reveal; solo memories use centered vertical cards; the Neha and Kaustubh portrait is enlarged and vertically raised while the carousel arrows remain on the existing higher layer, and Anya's paired collage uses two framed images; the compact venue page arranges ceremonial symbols, a reduced-height baraat band, mirrored akshada ornaments, fact rows, a small muted parking note within the address row, and responsive Maps action within the floral frame; reduced-motion is supported
script.js: the marriage announcement reveals the wedding framing once per conversation and replay resets it; invitee autoplay follows father, mother, Neha and Kaustubh, Kaku-Dada-Vahini, cats, then Anya; the final venue section is scrolled to its top instead of centered so the preceding page is not left above the viewport; Bappa-focus clears the preceding couple scene
script.js logging review: no logging calls required for deterministic presentation timing or carousel selection; wake-lock rejection remains intentionally silent as a non-critical browser enhancement
